WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.834
The family of a North

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.368
Carolina

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.936
man is suing Google,

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.971
accusing the tech giant of negligence

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.773
after their loved one died

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.942
allegedly because of Google Maps.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:09.676
Phillip Jackson's

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.677
wife says her husband

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.512
was driving back home from her daughter's

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.280
birthday party last summer.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.515
His family says he was following

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:15.915
the app's

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.151
GPS directions on a dark and rainy night,

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.219
which led him to

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.221
an unmarked, collapsed bridge

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.056
that he assumed was a safe route

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.457
because of the GPS directions.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.026
This is what the bridge looked like

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.027
in the daytime.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.095
Instead, he fell to his death.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.231
The lawsuit claims Google had received

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.432
notifications from area

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.034
residents about the bridge,

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.269
but failed to update its maps.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.737
Now, Google has issued a statement

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.138
that reads,

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.572
We have the deepest sympathies

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.940
for the Jackson family.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.542
Our goal is to provide accurate

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.411
routing information in maps,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.479
and we are reviewing this lawsuit.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.881
The family is also suing

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.015
Google's parent company,

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.117
Alphabet and two local companies

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.986
for failing to maintain the bridge.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.521
CNN has asked for comment

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.389
from those co-defendants as well.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.023
So joining me

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.825
now is Alisha

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.261
Jackson, Phillip Jackson's widow.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.898
Alicia, I just want to start with one.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.466
I'm so sorry for your loss.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.401
I'm so sorry that this happened,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.302
but that your husband

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:09.669
was leaving

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.870
your daughter's birthday party.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.405
You had left earlier.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.673
What did you think

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.508
when she didn't come home?

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.377
How did you tell your two daughters

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.347
Well, I thought

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.015
first that

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.883
he was sleeping on the couch

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.119
when I woke up, so I didn't really rush.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.754
But when I came downstairs,

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.355
saw he wasn't there,

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.657
and I was kind of confused.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.925
And my daughter came down

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.393
and asked, where's daddy?

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.795
And I said, I don't know.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.697
And she started to cry.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.299
So I said, no, no, it's okay, honey.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.100
You know, Daddy,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.368
I'm sure he's helping somebody now.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:42.902
He does.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.105
Somebody needed to use the truck.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.906
And then I kind of went in the back room

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.476
and started calling my friends and

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:50.844
asking when he left.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.078
And they

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.546
said, we'll drive the roads

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:56.649
to see if we can find him or anything.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.051
I call the police.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:58.818
They said, No, no way.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.920
I'm telling anybody, don't worry,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.056
you know, and I check the hospitals.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.425
Then a while later,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:07.694
Amelia I.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:08.428
My daughter, she

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:11.064
knocked on the door and said, Mommy,

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.532
the police are here.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.567
And immediately, my

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.169
my heart just hit the floor.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.938
And I was on the phone with his sister,

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.240
and she told me, just breathe.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:20.940
Just breathe.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.742
And I went out and,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:22.976
you know,

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.010
the police were there

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.411
and all of my friends

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.480
and just the look on their faces

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.414
you know, I just knew

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.183
and it felt like

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.685
forever that they weren't telling me

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.354
that, you know, and I was kind of like,

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.456
what's crazy? Where is he?

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.891
And so then

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.092
it was the worst day of my life.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.960
I just started, like,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.195
of course, right now.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.730
And then in the midst of it,

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.298
my girls are coming to the door

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.866
trying to see if I'm okay.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:47.700
Because they can hear me.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.002
So I'm trying to say this.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.603
Okay, go back inside.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.504
And then my friend said,

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.172
you know, you just

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.373
you just have to tell them.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:56.943
And I just went inside, and I told them,

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:57.377
you know,

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.811
girls know Daddy

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.481
had an accident and he went to heaven,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.283
but those are our dog. And

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.519
my youngest is sort of in shock.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.954
The oldest.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.156
Very, very smart. Very.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:10.356
I mean,

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.391
they're both very close with them,

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:14.627
but she just got very angry

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.762
and just started

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:16.629
running around

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.764
and pushing everything

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.666
off of the countertops.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.568
And, you know, understandably

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:24.571
and I try to give her a hug, said,

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.238
I don't want a hug.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.239
I want daddy you know?

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.006
She said,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.975
what are we going to do on Father's Day?

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.310
I don't want to get married.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.711
He's not going to be there.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:36.816
And so it's you know, it was hard yeah.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:40.620
And I had to, you know, just to go ahead,

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.655
I was going to say about Raymond,

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.323
you know,

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.558
I can't imagine your loss

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.726
I just want to say that.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.127
And to even have a daughter

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.462
looking that far ahead

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:50.430
to her wedding day,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.931
I can't imagine as well.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.933
I want to bring in your attorney,

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.868
Robert Zimmerman.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.970
Robert,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.771
we read a little bit of Google statement

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.073
saying they have the deepest sympathies

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.107
for the family.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.276
But but lay it out for us here.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.311
Why one?

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:05.545
Do you have

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:06.713
any reaction to that statement?

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.280
But also,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.848
why are you all suing

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.017
Google and specifically for what

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:13.753
Sure.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:14.954
And thanks for having us.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.389
We are suing essentially

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.490
two groups of defendants.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.559
This was a private road

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.160
and we are suing those responsible

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.095
for the road.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.263
This was a development

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.832
that was built about three

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.000
or four decades ago.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.035
And when they built that development,

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:30.403
they sold the houses.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.471
But their responsibility

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.505
didn't stop there.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:33.906
They had a responsibility to either

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.875
turn the roads over to the North

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.210
Carolina Department

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.344
of Transportation

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.178
or set up

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.014
an adequate maintenance program.

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.315
And they did neither

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.483
And this was a bridge

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.317
that no one in

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:44.917
the community

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.287
wanted to take responsibility for

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.255
with respect to Google.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.923
Google was aware for years

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.325
before this incident

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.227
that this bridge had collapsed

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:55.561
and there was essentially

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.195
a cliff

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.630
and a crater in the middle

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.699
of a residential neighborhood

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.467
for nine years.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.969
There is no good reason

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.904
why this could occur.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.307
And we have evidence that

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.843
multiple complaints were made to Google

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.212
through their Google Maps application,

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.315
telling them that this was an issue,

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:17.817
telling them that there were articles

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:20.386
that showed that this bridge was out

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.921
and they did nothing

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:22.922
I appreciate

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.491
they have sympathy at this time,

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:28.661
but it never should have allowed

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.529
it never should have been allowed

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.230
to occur for this long.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.866
And Alicia, obviously,

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.536
GPS is a major part of anyone's life

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.504
who's driving on the roads.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:39.372
Are you able

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.407
do you feel you're able to trust

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:42.842
GPS again?

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.644
Or how do you view

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:45.945
whipping that out to use it

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:49.082
now, given what what we're learning here

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.286
Well, there's sort of

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:54.654
no other choice

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:57.557
these days rather than to use GPS.

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.460
And so I have to use it.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.228
But I'm kind of

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.396
cynical, like,

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:05.131
well, just be careful, you know, don't,

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:06.833
you know,

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:10.203
drive off anything that's, you know,

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.337
that not there.

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.538
I mean, I've got to angry about it,

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.706
but I still have to use it.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:16.209
So it's always in the back of my mind.

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.511
But that's the thing is that everybody

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:19.779
trusts it.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:22.148
And or at least has to rely on it.

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:25.151
So I think that it needs to be safe

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.252
or at least

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:28.921
to the best of the makers ability.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:29.522
Yeah.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.524
Well, Alicia Paxson, Robert Zimmerman,

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:33.126
thank you for joining us, Alicia.

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.861
Again, so sorry for your loss.

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.262
We'll continue to follow this case.

